     9	\label{ch:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_A_1}
    10	
    11	\paragraph{Problem source.}
    12	Two water reservoirs are separated by a vertical wall MN.  A square slot of
    13	vertical size a*sqrt(2)/2 is sealed by a fully submerged solid cube of side a
    14	and density 3*rho\_0, where rho\_0 is the density of water.  The cube is hinged
    15	frictionlessly at O and may rotate about an axis perpendicular to the figure.
    16	The maximum permitted difference in water levels is Delta h = 1.41 m.  Use
    17	Figure 1a on the source page for the exact geometry and lever arms.
    18	
    19	Current subquestion:
    20	Calculate the side length a that makes Delta h = 1.41 m the maximum permissible water-level difference.
    21	
    22	\paragraph{Current subquestion.}
    23	Calculate the side length a that makes Delta h = 1.41 m the maximum permissible water-level difference.
    24	
    25	\paragraph{Recorded answer/context.}
    26	a = Delta h/(2*sqrt(2)) = 0.50 m.
